# {{.SudoEnvFile}}: what a brokered command's sudo is given, on top of what sudo
# builds for it.
#
# Written by the install when it grants sudo, and REWRITTEN BY EVERY RUN. Removed
# by a re-run that grants none, with the rest of the grant.
#
# sudoers reads this as part of the policy: root's, and never writable by the
# executor's uid, or that uid would be choosing root's environment. It is the
# other half of env_reset -- what the caller had is discarded, and what this
# names is put back from a file the caller cannot touch. A variable here is only
# added if sudo did not already set one, so HOME, PATH and SUDO_* stay sudo's.
#
# FARAMIR_OPERATOR is who the host belongs to. SUDO_USER cannot say it: sudo sets
# that from the account that invoked it, which for a brokered command is the
# executor, whose home holds none of the operator's configuration.
FARAMIR_OPERATOR={{.AgentUser}}
{{- range $name, $value := .CommandEnv}}
{{$name}}={{$value}}
{{- end}}
